wer.type/math :answer/value "46!" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d0d87553-dab1-5046-8598-8f79d15fc0d7" :question/id #uuid "d0d87553-dab1-5046-8598-8f79d15fc0d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-107849" :question/problem "Evaluate $Γ(6).$" :question/worked-solution "For any natural number $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nΓ(n)=(n-1)!.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nΓ(6)=5!=120.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-98f51cef-a29a-5755-8038-5da0f529bee9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-98f51cef-a29a-5755-8038-5da0f529bee9" :answer-field/id #uuid "98f51cef-a29a-5755-8038-5da0f529bee9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-91c7943b-a614-5f02-890f-e5dcc585e8ab" :answer-field/choices ["answer-91c7943b-a614-5f02-890f-e5dcc585e8ab" "answer-b4dbfe0d-5314-5022-91ea-56ae70315de5" "answer-5a3da224-1c13-581e-8e58-d2d8d7580f45" "answer-31575386-b43c-5cfb-b9cf-056d4be6aa3e" "answer-fa66fae1-bbae-5fc5-ad6f-3ee4976b2c3f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91c7943b-a614-5f02-890f-e5dcc585e8ab" :answer/id #uuid "91c7943b-a614-5f02-890f-e5dcc585e8ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "120" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4dbfe0d-5314-5022-91ea-56ae70315de5" :answer/id #uuid "b4dbfe0d-5314-5022-91ea-56ae70315de5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a3da224-1c13-581e-8e58-d2d8d7580f45" :answer/id #uuid "5a3da224-1c13-581e-8e58-d2d8d7580f45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "49" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31575386-b43c-5cfb-b9cf-056d4be6aa3e" :answer/id #uuid "31575386-b43c-5cfb-b9cf-056d4be6aa3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,040" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa66fae1-bbae-5fc5-ad6f-3ee4976b2c3f" :answer/id #uuid "fa66fae1-bbae-5fc5-ad6f-3ee4976b2c3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "720" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172231 :question/problem "Evaluate $Γ(\\frac{7}{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(\\frac{7}{2}) & =\\frac{5}{2}Γ(\\frac{5}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168249 :answer-field/correct "answer-680dd59f-269a-5239-be6c-db7639bc6aff" :answer-field/choices ["answer-afc4fe46-ebb9-53be-a4db-c19fc81cfcc0" "answer-680dd59f-269a-5239-be6c-db7639bc6aff" "answer-6c60091c-6a50-58f6-8506-d0161e3cbf8a" "answer-e8402d97-f15b-5b34-be19-f1b09c6f80c8" "answer-57f6601b-563c-5b31-a64c-7ec8c55ad32b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afc4fe46-ebb9-53be-a4db-c19fc81cfcc0" :answer/id #uuid "afc4fe46-ebb9-53be-a4db-c19fc81cfcc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{7}\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-680dd59f-269a-5239-be6c-db7639bc6aff" :answer/id #uuid "680dd59f-269a-5239-be6c-db7639bc6aff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c60091c-6a50-58f6-8506-d0161e3cbf8a" :answer/id #uuid "6c60091c-6a50-58f6-8506-d0161e3cbf8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8402d97-f15b-5b34-be19-f1b09c6f80c8" :answer/id #uuid "e8402d97-f15b-5b34-be19-f1b09c6f80c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{6}\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57f6601b-563c-5b31-a64c-7ec8c55ad32b" :answer/id #uuid "57f6601b-563c-5b31-a64c-7ec8c55ad32b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bd01511b-f45a-5cd4-b173-d099f3266062" :question/id #uuid "bd01511b-f45a-5cd4-b173-d099f3266062" :question/math-academy-id "q-107860" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\,Γ(\\frac{9}{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\,Γ(\\frac{9}{2}) & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot Γ(\\frac{7}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}Γ(\\frac{5}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\  & =7\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2e8f9836-3d65-5692-9b53-efc548319f0d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2e8f9836-3d65-5692-9b53-efc548319f0d" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e8f9836-3d65-5692-9b53-efc548319f0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fc7aaba3-9d2b-5078-921a-a7a5e7d7f864" :answer-field/choices ["answer-272b993d-cfcd-5fbc-8438-b2fc2453c336" "answer-fdf35405-2f8a-5450-8095-15a55e5e6172" "answer-87e9f7a5-e27e-53c0-8cae-d05da59ced47" "answer-fc7aaba3-9d2b-5078-921a-a7a5e7d7f864" "answer-5c4d0a3c-d3e6-501a-ae95-afa45890cb45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-272b993d-cfcd-5fbc-8438-b2fc2453c336" :answer/id #uuid "272b993d-cfcd-5fbc-8438-b2fc2453c336" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdf35405-2f8a-5450-8095-15a55e5e6172" :answer/id #uuid "fdf35405-2f8a-5450-8095-15a55e5e6172" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87e9f7a5-e27e-53c0-8cae-d05da59ced47" :answer/id #uuid "87e9f7a5-e27e-53c0-8cae-d05da59ced47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc7aaba3-9d2b-5078-921a-a7a5e7d7f864" :answer/id #uuid "fc7aaba3-9d2b-5078-921a-a7a5e7d7f864" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c4d0a3c-d3e6-501a-ae95-afa45890cb45" :answer/id #uuid "5c4d0a3c-d3e6-501a-ae95-afa45890cb45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6bbc8ec2-1cd6-5115-ab81-c2fbacd13746" :question/id #uuid "6bbc8ec2-1cd6-5115-ab81-c2fbacd13746" :question/math-academy-id "q-107855" :question/problem "Evaluate $4\\sqrt{\\pi }\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(\\frac{5}{2}) & =\\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{\\pi }}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n4\\sqrt{\\pi }\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=4\\sqrt{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }=3\\pi .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ecdcf851-bd5a-52f8-bfcc-45e6d82c2328"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ecdcf851-bd5a-52f8-bfcc-45e6d82c2328" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecdcf851-bd5a-52f8-bfcc-45e6d82c2328" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-179d6519-3f5e-5e5c-931a-bef96f2e6027" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bca03f9f-8e84-56ca-8ab2-759eaf4b56d1" "answer-179d6519-3f5e-5e5c-931a-bef96f2e6027" "answer-da7d5a9a-ce82-5886-ae3c-0b43836c92d1" "answer-823c273b-b579-5de8-8c66-72b5bee2d5a0" "answer-8245d4e4-4d9b-5e0f-9138-dddbd9735459"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bca03f9f-8e84-56ca-8ab2-759eaf4b56d1" :answer/id #uuid "bca03f9f-8e84-56ca-8ab2-759eaf4b56d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-179d6519-3f5e-5e5c-931a-bef96f2e6027" :answer/id #uuid "179d6519-3f5e-5e5c-931a-bef96f2e6027" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da7d5a9a-ce82-5886-ae3c-0b43836c92d1" :answer/id #uuid "da7d5a9a-ce82-5886-ae3c-0b43836c92d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi \\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-823c273b-b579-5de8-8c66-72b5bee2d5a0" :answer/id #uuid "823c273b-b579-5de8-8c66-72b5bee2d5a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8245d4e4-4d9b-5e0f-9138-dddbd9735459" :answer/id #uuid "8245d4e4-4d9b-5e0f-9138-dddbd9735459" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi \\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-38540fee-f0e4-596e-9eff-9715fa0a19af" :question/id #uuid "38540fee-f0e4-596e-9eff-9715fa0a19af" :question/math-academy-id "q-107886" :question/problem "$Γ(\\frac{7}{2})+Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(\\frac{7}{2}) & =\\frac{5}{2}\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\,Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nΓ(\\frac{7}{2})+Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{15}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }+\\sqrt{\\pi }=\\frac{23}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-af6e50ef-05cd-5170-9ca8-db0d80c3fd8a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-af6e50ef-05cd-5170-9ca8-db0d80c3fd8a" :answer-field/id #uuid "af6e50ef-05cd-5170-9ca8-db0d80c3fd8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b551f6da-f7c3-592b-9b70-c9a13bffd28c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-60a4904e-dcde-5ed0-889d-30606d3a21d2" "answer-b551f6da-f7c3-592b-9b70-c9a13bffd28c" "answer-5fecaf9c-523b-5840-82f6-4a073fed5f55" "answer-15b2ab14-edca-5f56-b447-4b5fab9c2703" "answer-5d513a95-f295-54c8-8a9c-aee17a71f839"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60a4904e-dcde-5ed0-889d-30606d3a21d2" :answer/id #uuid "60a4904e-dcde-5ed0-889d-30606d3a21d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b551f6da-f7c3-592b-9b70-c9a13bffd28c" :answer/id #uuid "b551f6da-f7c3-592b-9b70-c9a13bffd28c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{8}\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fecaf9c-523b-5840-82f6-4a073fed5f55" :answer/id #uuid "5fecaf9c-523b-5840-82f6-4a073fed5f55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15b2ab14-edca-5f56-b447-4b5fab9c2703" :answer/id #uuid "15b2ab14-edca-5f56-b447-4b5fab9c2703" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d513a95-f295-54c8-8a9c-aee17a71f839" :answer/id #uuid "5d513a95-f295-54c8-8a9c-aee17a71f839" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0fdfcf02-67ae-5263-baa1-a6ba5d9b1b6d" :question/id #uuid "0fdfcf02-67ae-5263-baa1-a6ba5d9b1b6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-107862" :question/problem "$Γ(\\frac{1}{2})+4\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=\\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2})=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi }=\\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nΓ(\\frac{1}{2})+4\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }+4\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }=4\\sqrt{\\pi }.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bb60e818-0b8f-5548-8ae0-4c03ecdde68e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bb60e818-0b8f-5548-8ae0-4c03ecdde68e" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb60e818-0b8f-5548-8ae0-4c03ecdde68e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b2a0e4e4-dd3b-55bc-a9fb-699bdd60de42" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b2a0e4e4-dd3b-55bc-a9fb-699bdd60de42" "answer-067a2195-d3de-5acc-b220-c39097febda2" "answer-45dd61c6-4646-5510-9b63-d54bc159f05b" "answer-d776aef3-e85d-5ab3-8ee3-9c9b560c8c22" "answer-d65e1e14-1f3f-5358-bf26-7ba446ad986d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2a0e4e4-dd3b-55bc-a9fb-699bdd60de42" :answer/id #uuid "b2a0e4e4-dd3b-55bc-a9fb-699bdd60de42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-067a2195-d3de-5acc-b220-c39097febda2" :answer/id #uuid "067a2195-d3de-5acc-b220-c39097febda2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45dd61c6-4646-5510-9b63-d54bc159f05b" :answer/id #uuid "45dd61c6-4646-5510-9b63-d54bc159f05b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d776aef3-e85d-5ab3-8ee3-9c9b560c8c22" :answer/id #uuid "d776aef3-e85d-5ab3-8ee3-9c9b560c8c22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d65e1e14-1f3f-5358-bf26-7ba446ad986d" :answer/id #uuid "d65e1e14-1f3f-5358-bf26-7ba446ad986d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173179 :tutorial/content "The **gamma function** $\\Gamma(z)$ extends the factorial function to positive real numbers and parts of the complex plane.\n\nIn particular, for any natural number $n \\geq 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(n) = (n-1)!\n$$\n\nIf the complex number $z$ satisfies $\\textrm{Re}(z) > 0,$ then the gamma function can be defined as the improper integral\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(z) = \\int_0^\\infty t^{z-1} e^{-t} \\, \\textrm dt.\n$$\n\nIn this lesson, we will only consider cases where $z$ is a positive real number." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173180 :tutorial/content "To evaluate the gamma function at positive integer multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(z+1) = z \\Gamma(z), \\qquad \\Gamma \\left( \\dfrac{1}{2} \\right) = \\sqrt{\\pi}\n$$\n\nWe'll prove these results at the end of the lesson." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173224 :tutorial/content "Here, we'll prove the recursive formula for the gamma function:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(z+1) = z \\Gamma(z)\n$$\n\nThe formula comes from applying integration by parts to the integral in the definition of the gamma function. By definition,\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(z) = \\int_0^\\infty t^{z-1} e^{-t} \\, \\textrm dt, \\qquad\\textrm{Re}(z) > 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(z+1) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{t}^{z}{e}^{-t}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }-z{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{t\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{{t}^{z}}{{e}^{t}})-{(-\\frac{{t}^{z}}{{e}^{t}})|}_{t=0}+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }z{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =0-0+z{{{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t}_{⏟}}_{Γ(z)} \\\\  & =zΓ(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173181 :tutorial/content "Previously, we used the following relationship between the gamma function and the factorial:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(n) = (n-1)!\n$$\n\nThis relationship holds for any natural number $n \\geq 1.$ Now, let's prove it.\n\nFirst, we start with the following identity, which we proved earlier:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(z+1) = z \\Gamma(z)\n$$\n\nFor any natural number $n \\geq 1,$ the above identity states the following:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(n+1) = n \\Gamma(n)\n$$\n\nNow, let's repeatedly expand out the right-hand side, noticing that most of the terms can be grouped into a factorial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(n+1) & =nΓ(n) \\\\  & =n\\cdot \\overset{Γ(n)}{\\overset{⏞}{(n-1)\\cdot Γ(n-1)}} \\\\  & =n\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot \\overset{Γ(n-1)}{\\overset{⏞}{(n-2)\\cdot Γ(n-2)}} \\\\  & =… \\\\  & ={{n\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot (n-2)\\cdot …\\cdot 1}_{⏟}}_{n!}\\cdot Γ(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(n+1) = n! \\cdot \\Gamma(1).\n$$\n\nTo evaluate $\\Gamma(1),$ we can use the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(1) = \\int_0^\\infty e^{-t} \\, \\textrm dt = 1\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(n+1) = n!\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173182 :tutorial/content "Previously, we used the fact that $\\Gamma \\left( \\dfrac{1}{2} \\right) = \\sqrt{\\pi}.$ To prove this, we can directly compute the value of $\\Gamma \\left( \\dfrac{1}{2} \\right)$ using the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = \\int_0^\\infty t^{-1/2} e^{-t} \\, \\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe simplify this integral using the substitution $t = u^2,$ which implies $\\text{d}t = 2u \\, \\text{d}u.$ Also, note that $u \\to 0^+$ as $t \\to 0^+$ and $u \\to \\infty$ as $t \\to \\infty.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nt^{-1/2} e^{-t} \\, \\text{d}t = (u^2)^{-1/2} e^{-u^2} \\cdot 2u \\, \\text{d}u = e^{-u^2} \\cdot 2 \\, \\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nThus, we get\n\n$$\n\\Gamma\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = \\int_0^\\infty t^{-1/2} e^{-t} \\, \\text{d}t = 2 \\int_0^\\infty e^{-u^2} \\, \\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nThis is directly related to the well-known **Gaussian integral**:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty e^{-u^2} \\, \\text{d}u = \\sqrt{\\pi}\n$$\n\nSince the integrand $e^{-u^2}$ is even (i.e., symmetric about the $y$-axis), we have\n\n$$\n\\int_0^\\infty e^{-u^2} \\, \\text{d}u = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty e^{-u^2} \\, \\text{d}u = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\sqrt{\\pi}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into our expression for the Gamma function, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\Gamma\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{2} \\sqrt{\\pi} = \\sqrt{\\pi}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172142 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
